<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  DEV-FLAVOR + DEBUG-BUILD-TYPE ONLY. Android Gradle Plugin only merges src/devDebug/** into the
  devDebug variant (applicationId com.budcom.android.dev.debug); it is structurally absent from
  every other variant, including prodDebug (com.budcom.android.debug, the pre-existing installation)
  and every release build. See app/build.gradle.kts's own "DEV isolation" comment for why devDebug
  is a distinct, coexisting application id that never touches an existing installation's package or
  data.

  This declares ONE narrowly-scoped broadcast receiver that lets a local controlled pilot automation
  script (scripts/budcom-controlled-pilot.ps1, run over adb from the same machine the developer
  already controls) trigger a real enrollment attempt without a manual UI tap; see
  PilotEnrollmentReceiver's own doc comment for exactly what it does and does not do.

  exported="true" is deliberate, not an oversight: on current Android (verified against a real
  device, API 36), `adb shell am broadcast -n` cannot reliably reach a non-exported explicit
  component even from the privileged `shell` UID, and a signature-level custom permission would be
  self-defeating here (adb's `shell` UID is not signed with this app's key, so it could never hold
  such a permission -- that would just break the orchestration script's own ability to call this).
  This does NOT meaningfully widen the attack surface: there is no <intent-filter>, so the receiver
  is not discoverable via any implicit broadcast; the Intent itself carries no extras and no secret
  material (the grant lives only in this app's own already-sandboxed private storage, unreachable by
  any other app without root); and the only action a co-located app could ever trigger is "re-read
  whatever is already sitting in your own private files directory" -- which it has no way to have
  written in the first place. Compiled out of every build except devDebug regardless.
-->
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <application>
        <receiver
            android:name="com.budcom.android.pilotharness.PilotEnrollmentReceiver"
            android:exported="true" />
    </application>
</manifest>
